Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC18, AC19, AC23, AC26, AC36)
ADR: docs/decisions/0003-reverseproxy-with-rewrite-as-proxy-engine.md
Research: Q6 (delete upstream X-Request-Id), Q7 (chi wrapper keeps Flush)
Why this approach: ModifyResponse strips Proxy-*, deletes upstream's X-Request-Id, sets Meta.Stream from the parsed media type (parameters ignored), Meta.TTFB from a new unexported Meta.start set in ServeHTTP, and wraps res.Body in the T6 response watcher; the Meta is found through res.Request's context. FlushInterval is -1. Building it showed net/http sniffs a Content-Type for a response upstream sent without one; with FlushInterval -1 the stdlib's initial header flush usually wins that race, but not always, so ServeHTTP puts an empty Content-Type entry on the writer when it has none, which stops the sniff outright (plan.md "Response hook" updated).
Alternatives rejected: setting the gateway's ID in ModifyResponse (ReverseProxy adds with Header.Add, giving two, Q6); relying on FlushInterval's header-flush timer to avoid sniffing (a race).
Trade-off / known limit: core names no provider, so TestProxy_UpstreamErrorsVerbatim uses neutral X-Ratelimit-* headers for AC26's anthropic-ratelimit-* family; every header name is treated alike. The empty Content-Type entry stays only if nothing else sets one; T10's error handler will use Set.
Verified by: TestProxy_ResponseVerbatim (no-Content-Type case), TestProxy_GatewayRequestIDWinsOnResponse, TestProxy_FlushIntervalIsImmediate and TestAccessLog_ProxyFields first failed for the right reasons (sniffed text/html, two X-Request-Id values, FlushInterval 0, no stream/ttfb_ms); TestProxy_StreamsSSEWithoutBuffering and TestProxy_UpstreamErrorsVerbatim passed on arrival and were proved by temporary mutations (io.ReadAll in ModifyResponse, and a writer wrapper hiding Flush, each timed out the SSE read; deleting Retry-After failed the errors test); removing the empty Content-Type entry with FlushInterval 0 failed ResponseVerbatim, all reverted; go test -race -count=3 ./internal/core ./internal/server; make verify.

Follow-up: Q17 (net/http Content-Type sniffing) and Q18 (where AC26's literal anthropic-ratelimit-* proof lives) were recorded in research.md in d89a736, after this commit.
